# Hand-authored SPL (not compiled by pySigma; pySigma cannot express this
# at all, see evidence/18_negation_sqlite_compile.txt). SPL can express
# "principal X made zero qualifying RC4 TGS requests" directly because
# `stats` can be told to enumerate the UNIVERSE of principals from a
# separate, wider search (e.g. all Kerberos activity, or a lookup of known
# service accounts) and left-join/append qualifying-event counts onto it,
# rather than only ever being able to GROUP BY existing rows in the
# filtered result set. This is the SPL-side half of the same negation
# comparison whose Sigma-side half is proven impossible in
# scripts/04_prove_correlation_cannot_express_absence.py.
#
# This query was NOT run against live Splunk (auth unavailable, see
# evidence/05_splunk_auth_attempt.txt); it is presented as the SPL-side
# construct that pySigma's correlation compiler has no equivalent for, not
# as an executed result.

`wineventlog_security` EventCode=4769
| stats count(eval(TicketEncryptionType="0x17")) as rc4_count by TargetUserName
| where rc4_count=0
